      "text": "We know that $\\sin (\\pi + \\theta) = -\\sin (\\theta)$.\nThis means that $\\sin \\frac{11 \\pi}{3} = \\sin \\left(\\pi + \\frac{4 \\pi}{3}\\right) = -\\sin \\frac{4 \\pi}{3}$.\nThe tangent of an angle can be found using the identity $\\tan (\\pi + \\theta) = \\tan (\\theta)$.\nSo, $\\tan \\frac{4 \\pi}{3} = \\tan \\left(\\pi + \\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right) = \\tan \\frac{\\pi}{3}$.\nWe know that $\\tan \\frac{\\pi}{3} = \\frac{\\sin \\frac{\\pi}{3}}{\\cos \\frac{\\pi}{3}} = \\frac{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}}{\\frac{1}{2}} = \\sqrt{3}$.\nFinally, $\\sin \\frac{4 \\pi}{3} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$.\nTherefore, $\\sin \\frac{11 \\pi}{3} = -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$.\nThe answer is: -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}",
